didn't c2c list used to show nodes grouped by repo? We should have a way to list all c2c nodes on the machine

Resolution (2026-07-16): already supported by `c2c list --global` (`-g`).
The command scans every known per-repository broker root on the machine and
groups human output into current/other repository sections. Live dogfood
confirmed grouped output, the CLI help and `docs/commands.md` document the
flag, and the focused `test_c2c_find` suite covers filtering, `--all`, JSON,
and repository grouping (15 tests passed). The repo-local default is retained
to avoid changing established output and high-frequency agent workflows.
